WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.149 --> 00:00:07.231
Hey Thoughty2 here. Do you know what you’re
eating? I mean, do you really know? Because

00:00:07.231 --> 00:00:13.389
you may think you do, but you’ve been lied
to your entire life. Now this may be hard

00:00:13.389 --> 00:00:20.089
to stomach, but a lot of the food you eat
is fake. Okay, this is not true for everyone

00:00:20.089 --> 00:00:24.759
watching. Different countries have vastly
different food regulations and some countries

00:00:24.759 --> 00:00:29.939
are far, far worse offenders at dishing up
fake food to its citizens, I’ll reveal the

00:00:29.939 --> 00:00:36.320
worst countries for doing this in a minute
but first let’s take a jar of harmless honey.

00:00:36.320 --> 00:00:42.700
It’s touted as one of nature’s superfoods,
it can prevent cancer and heart disease. It’s

00:00:42.700 --> 00:00:50.380
a powerful probiotic and it boosts your immune
system. And all of that is true, if you’re

00:00:50.380 --> 00:00:55.440
eating real honey that is. Germany is the
world’s largest importer of honey; those

00:00:55.440 --> 00:01:01.800
Germans love their honey! But the world’s
second largest honey importer, America tells

00:01:01.800 --> 00:01:08.640
a different story when it comes to this supposedly
wholly natural product. A study found that

00:01:08.640 --> 00:01:16.790
over 75% of honey sold in the US doesn’t
contain any honey. According to the FDA, honey

00:01:16.790 --> 00:01:22.700
has to contain pollen, otherwise it isn’t
honey. It was discovered that the vast majority

00:01:22.700 --> 00:01:28.820
of commercial honey brands on the shelves
of American stores contained no pollen at

00:01:28.820 --> 00:01:32.960
all and therefore were not actually honey
at all.

00:01:32.960 --> 00:01:39.380
So if all this honey isn’t honey, then what
is it? Well there are many different, carefully

00:01:39.380 --> 00:01:45.860
engineered cocktails of artificial ingredients
that are used to replicate real honey and

00:01:45.860 --> 00:01:51.630
each producer uses their own unique mixture.
Most are mainly made up from the infamous

00:01:51.630 --> 00:01:58.030
high-fructose corn syrup, sometimes labelled
as Maltitol syrup, cut with sucrose syrup

00:01:58.030 --> 00:02:04.850
and water. Sometimes some plant extracts and
essential oils are thrown in there, if you’re

00:02:04.850 --> 00:02:09.689
lucky. So you thought you were being healthy
by swapping your pancake syrup for honey,

00:02:09.689 --> 00:02:13.720
but in reality it’s probably the exact same
thing.

00:02:13.720 --> 00:02:20.969
So why do American honey producers sell billions
of dollar’s worth of artificial sugars labelled

00:02:20.969 --> 00:02:29.549
as honey? Simple economics; real honey is
expensive, just think about what has to happen

00:02:29.549 --> 00:02:37.170
to make honey. Bees have to visit 2 million
flowers to produce just one cup of honey,

00:02:37.170 --> 00:02:43.970
travelling 55,000 miles in the process. And
over its entire lifetime a single bee will

00:02:43.970 --> 00:02:48.349
produce just half a teaspoon of honey.

00:02:48.349 --> 00:02:53.760
High-fructose corn syrup and other similar
ingredients are incredibly cheap to produce

00:02:53.760 --> 00:03:01.700
and so companies can sell fake honey for much
cheaper to consumers, who are non-the-wiser.

00:03:01.700 --> 00:03:06.930
There are also no regulations in place in
America concerning the actual percentage of

00:03:06.930 --> 00:03:14.260
real honey-content required. In Europe there
are very strict rules about what can be labelled

00:03:14.260 --> 00:03:20.781
and sold as honey. European regulations dictate
that anything sold as “honey” must contain

00:03:20.781 --> 00:03:31.449
at least 60% actual honey and cannot contain
more than 5% sucrose, i.e. syrups. The vast

00:03:31.449 --> 00:03:37.000
majority of honey sold across Europe was found
to be 100% honey.

00:03:37.000 --> 00:03:42.620
Through no fault of their own American’s
are also not use to the idea that honey crystalizes

00:03:42.620 --> 00:03:49.420
very quickly and 100% raw honey will usually
already be highly crystalized when you take

00:03:49.420 --> 00:03:57.449
it off the shelf. Honey never spoils and crystallization
is completely normal, after all, it is a sugar

00:03:57.449 --> 00:04:03.689
and sugar just loves to crystalize. Europeans
have always been sold crystalized honey and

00:04:03.689 --> 00:04:10.180
so, are use to the idea. A survey found that
most American’s would wrongly consider crystalized

00:04:10.180 --> 00:04:16.079
honey to be spoilt. But when you’re selling
syrups disguised as honey, you don’t have

00:04:16.079 --> 00:04:19.280
to worry about crystallization.

00:04:19.280 --> 00:04:27.490
2.3 Billion cups of coffee are drank around
the world every day but what goes into your

00:04:27.490 --> 00:04:34.550
cup? Let me guess, ground coffee or instant
coffee (if you’re an animal), hot water,

00:04:34.550 --> 00:04:40.490
then maybe milk or cream and perhaps some
sugar. Oh and of course, let’s not forget

00:04:40.490 --> 00:04:48.729
the wheat, soybeans, seeds, corn, twigs and
dirt. Yes, you heard me correctly, your ground

00:04:48.729 --> 00:04:54.210
coffee, which should just be coffee and nothing
else, surely? …actually contains a whole

00:04:54.210 --> 00:05:01.900
array of fillers and more often than not these
fillers contain twigs and dirt. Well you did

00:05:01.900 --> 00:05:05.990
say you like coffees with an earthy flavour.

00:05:05.990 --> 00:05:11.729
Coffee is in trouble, big trouble. Coffee
is very sensitive, it doesn’t like being

00:05:11.729 --> 00:05:17.210
called names, but it’s also very picky about
where it’s grown. The plant will only produce

00:05:17.210 --> 00:05:23.730
coffee seeds, known to us all as coffee beans,
in humid, and very altitudinous mountainous

00:05:23.730 --> 00:05:29.569
areas. According to several experts, climate
change is threatening these sensitive environments

00:05:29.569 --> 00:05:37.030
and forecasts show that by 2050, half of the
regions in the world where coffee can be grown

00:05:37.030 --> 00:05:48.539
will be lost and by 2080 coffee could go extinct.
Due to growing fears, some unscrupulous ground

00:05:48.539 --> 00:05:54.139
coffee manufacturers have resorted to padding
out their coffee using fillers such as soybeans,

00:05:54.139 --> 00:05:57.599
acai seeds, brown sugar, barley and corn.

00:05:57.599 --> 00:06:03.729
Some by-products of coffee production that
should be removed from the final product are

00:06:03.729 --> 00:06:12.009
also purposely being left in to fill it out.
Such as wood, twigs, parchment, husks and

00:06:12.009 --> 00:06:18.030
even soil. If you buy whole beans then don’t
worry, there won’t be any fillers in there.

00:06:18.030 --> 00:06:23.250
Brazilian scientists were so concerned about
this that they developed a brand new technique

00:06:23.250 --> 00:06:29.210
using liquid chromatography&nbsp;and&nbsp;statistical
analysis that allowed them to detect exactly

00:06:29.210 --> 00:06:37.969
what percentage of a bag of ground coffee
is actual coffee. The procedure is 95% accurate.

00:06:37.969 --> 00:06:42.770
What they discovered was that some brands
of ground coffee have such a high percentage

00:06:42.770 --> 00:06:50.340
of fillers in them that they must be purposely
added in, there’s no way it’s an accident.

00:06:50.340 --> 00:06:57.580
If coffee isn’t your thing, then maybe orange
juice is. You may have been told many times

00:06:57.580 --> 00:07:03.890
that most orange juices are artificial, but
do you really know just how artificial? What

00:07:03.890 --> 00:07:11.630
if I told you that the flavour of most major
orange juice brands is 100% fake? To make

00:07:11.630 --> 00:07:18.039
orange juice you squeeze oranges right? Maybe
throw in some preservatives and added sugar.

00:07:18.039 --> 00:07:25.830
No, that would just be too easy for big brand
orange juices! They squeeze oranges then remove

00:07:25.830 --> 00:07:32.400
all the oxygen from the extracted juice, this
allows the juice to keep for a year without

00:07:32.400 --> 00:07:39.780
spoiling, yes your morning juice is anywhere
from a few months to a year old. But that’s

00:07:39.780 --> 00:07:47.580
not all that removing oxygen does, it also
removes all of the natural flavour and I mean

00:07:47.580 --> 00:07:53.270
all of it. So you’re left with a very old,
completely tasteless liquid that slightly

00:07:53.270 --> 00:07:56.750
resembles something that came out of an orange
once.

00:07:56.750 --> 00:08:04.289
The orange flavour is then artificially re-added
to the juice using a concoction of artificial

00:08:04.289 --> 00:08:10.570
flavourings. But why purposely remove the
flavour then put it in again, if it only makes

00:08:10.570 --> 00:08:18.699
it worse? I mean that’s not easy or cheap
to do. It’s all about consistency, each

00:08:18.699 --> 00:08:25.379
big brand orange juice has their own unique
flavour that customers are very familiar with.

00:08:25.379 --> 00:08:31.030
Imagine if the taste of Tropicana changed
slightly, millions of people would notice.

00:08:31.030 --> 00:08:38.280
The natural flavour from oranges is just not
consistent enough to stick a brand name on

00:08:38.280 --> 00:08:43.750
it and have people associate that flavour
with that particular brand, because the flavour

00:08:43.750 --> 00:08:49.470
would constantly change, depending on the
variety, location of the oranges and time

00:08:49.470 --> 00:08:51.090
of year.

00:08:51.090 --> 00:08:56.630
Orange juice manufacturers spend millions
hiring flavour and fragrance experts. The

00:08:56.630 --> 00:09:03.170
very same people that work for large perfume
companies, to create a unique and recognisable

00:09:03.170 --> 00:09:12.310
orange-juice-like flavour, just for their
product. The worst part is that the flavourings

00:09:12.310 --> 00:09:18.250
don’t even have to be listed under the ingredients,
because they’re derived from orange oils.

00:09:18.250 --> 00:09:23.300
Which is a dubious claim, but it technically
means these artificially flavoured drinks

00:09:23.300 --> 00:09:27.390
can be sold as 100% orange juice.

00:09:27.390 --> 00:09:34.430
So I bet you’re wondering which of your
favourite foods I’m going to ruin next.

00:09:34.430 --> 00:09:40.680
What about a simple steak? “No! Not the
steak!” A steak is just a single cut of

00:09:40.680 --> 00:09:47.590
beef right? What could possibly be suspicious
about that? Well if you opt for cheaper steaks,

00:09:47.590 --> 00:09:53.250
whether it be from the supermarket or even
your local butcher, you could be eating tens

00:09:53.250 --> 00:10:00.680
of different cows in a single steak. You’re
purchasing Frankenstein steaks that have actually

00:10:00.680 --> 00:10:06.930
been glued together from a whole array of
offcuts. And this doesn’t just happen with

00:10:06.930 --> 00:10:12.080
beef, it could be lamb, pork, venison, or
any meat really.

00:10:12.080 --> 00:10:17.090
When many animals are being turned into various
types of small food products, ready to throw

00:10:17.090 --> 00:10:22.500
into a pan at home, a lot of waste is created
and general chunks of meat that would most

00:10:22.500 --> 00:10:29.170
likely get thrown away. Some unscrupulous
companies and butchers use a meat glue called

00:10:29.170 --> 00:10:35.680
“transglutaminase”, that’s well known
within the food industry and completely untraceable

00:10:35.680 --> 00:10:42.510
within the final product. They basically glue
together the leftover pieces, which could

00:10:42.510 --> 00:10:50.780
have come from many different cows, to create
a Frankenstein steak, for your enjoyment.

00:10:50.780 --> 00:10:55.970
Transglutaminase is so good at fusing meat
together it would take an expert to examine

00:10:55.970 --> 00:11:02.810
a steak closely to detect any wrong doing.
The best part? It’s not a legal requirement

00:11:02.810 --> 00:11:09.660
to list it as an ingredient. So to be safe,
just stay away from cheap steaks, but what

00:11:09.660 --> 00:11:17.540
if you already do? Maybe you are a cow connoisseur
who opts to spend 40, 50 or even 100 dollars

00:11:17.540 --> 00:11:23.670
or more on a single steak in a restaurant.
And your favourite steak of all is the very

00:11:23.670 --> 00:11:31.810
pricey Kobe beef. The Kobe beef craze has
taken America in particular, by storm. Thousands

00:11:31.810 --> 00:11:39.360
of restaurants all over the country and many
large chains now offer highly-priced Kobe

00:11:39.360 --> 00:11:45.220
beef burgers, Kobe steaks and other Kobe beef
products on their menus.

00:11:45.220 --> 00:11:51.140
Kobe beef comes from Kobe cows, a breed of
Wagyu cattle that comes from Japan. The steaks

00:11:51.140 --> 00:11:56.780
they produce are prized by chefs the world
over for their impressive fat-marbling, flavour,

00:11:56.780 --> 00:12:05.150
and melt-in-your-mouth texture. It is the
ultimate steak. But it’s incredibly exclusive,

00:12:05.150 --> 00:12:11.380
Kobe beef can only come from Japan and just
3,000 cattle are deemed worthy enough to be

00:12:11.380 --> 00:12:20.060
slaughtered and turned into Kobe beef each
year. They are all fathered by just 12 highly-prized

00:12:20.060 --> 00:12:24.690
bulls, that are considered “genetically
ideal”. Sounds to me like they’re trying

00:12:24.690 --> 00:12:31.890
to create a cow master-race over there. Kobe
cows are fed beer and sake to improve flavour.

00:12:31.890 --> 00:12:38.510
Every cow is massaged daily to improve fat
marbling. Hell, I want to be a Kobe cow.

00:12:38.510 --> 00:12:44.810
That’s some serious dedication to creating
a tasty steak and it doesn’t come cheap,

00:12:44.810 --> 00:12:52.920
it varies but it will cost you on average
about $350 to eat a real Kobe steak in a restaurant.

00:12:52.920 --> 00:12:58.380
Because supplies are purposely kept small
to focus on quality, the amount of real Kobe

00:12:58.380 --> 00:13:08.100
beef that reaches the US each year would only
feed 77 Americans. Yet millions of Americans

00:13:08.100 --> 00:13:13.560
are going out and regularly eating Kobe beef
in restaurants and buying it from the store

00:13:13.560 --> 00:13:20.830
to cook at home, for far, far less than $350
per steak. So what’s going on here?

00:13:20.830 --> 00:13:27.300
It’s one of the biggest food scams in America’s
history. As you have probably guessed by now,

00:13:27.300 --> 00:13:34.790
the vast, vast majority of so-called Kobe
beef sold in America is just plain old regular

00:13:34.790 --> 00:13:40.950
beef, that has never even been to Japan. It’s
just outright lying and clever marketing,

00:13:40.950 --> 00:13:48.980
if you can call it clever. Some farms in America
are now creating fake Kobe beef for much cheaper,

00:13:48.980 --> 00:13:55.320
often called “Faux-be beef” by those in
the know. This fake Kobe is sold in thousands

00:13:55.320 --> 00:14:04.180
of restaurants for upwards of $100 a steak.
But in reality there are only 9 restaurants

00:14:04.180 --> 00:14:13.500
in America that sell real Kobe beef, imported
from Japan; yes, just 9 and they have a special

00:14:13.500 --> 00:14:17.490
license, allowing them to cook and sell it.

00:14:17.490 --> 00:14:24.520
The fake food you consume in the average day
is sickening. Your olive oil is actually peanut

00:14:24.520 --> 00:14:32.620
oil, soyabean oil and palm oil. Your cheese
and even bread contains wood pulp, yes wood

00:14:32.620 --> 00:14:38.800
pulp, which the FDA says is safe to eat. Thanks
for the advice, but last time I checked I

00:14:38.800 --> 00:14:46.590
wasn’t a beaver. Your dried spices contain
a large amount of garden weeds. Your tea contains

00:14:46.590 --> 00:14:50.970
sawdust and sand.

00:14:50.970 --> 00:14:57.400
Blueberries are often faked, most products
containing blueberries, such as muffins, cereals

00:14:57.400 --> 00:15:05.470
and pancakes contain precisely zero blueberries.
Real blueberries are expensive and so food

00:15:05.470 --> 00:15:12.200
scientists have perfected a recipe of sugar,
purple dye and other questionable ingredients

00:15:12.200 --> 00:15:18.510
to craft imitation blueberries, with no health
benefits whatsoever.

00:15:18.510 --> 00:15:24.740
In America most of the Champagne sold is not
actually Champagne, most people believe that

00:15:24.740 --> 00:15:29.930
it’s illegal to sell sparkling wine as “Champagne”
if it doesn’t originate from the Champagne

00:15:29.930 --> 00:15:36.190
province in France and produced is using the
“Méthode Champenoise”, a second fermentation

00:15:36.190 --> 00:15:45.190
within the bottle. Well yes, this is true,
in every country in the World, except America.

00:15:45.190 --> 00:15:52.240
A 100-year-old legal loophole allows any American
sparkling wine, a simple bottle of Californian

00:15:52.240 --> 00:16:02.221
bubbly for example, to be sold as Champagne
within America. Do this in any other country

00:16:02.221 --> 00:16:08.170
and French lawsuits would take your fake Champers
off the shelves faster than you can say “Is

00:16:08.170 --> 00:16:11.710
this the bloody French inquisition or what…”

00:16:11.710 --> 00:16:17.340
Of course all of this changes depending on
where you live in the World. Every country

00:16:17.340 --> 00:16:23.970
has its own unique food regulations and different
levels of food quality. But which countries

00:16:23.970 --> 00:16:29.900
have the most fake food and which have the
least? British charity, Oxfam conducted a

00:16:29.900 --> 00:16:36.360
study comparing the quality of food in every
country in the World. The best countries in

00:16:36.360 --> 00:16:42.070
the world overall for food quality, and lack
of food-related health issues were found to

00:16:42.070 --> 00:16:52.330
be The Netherlands, France, Switzerland, Denmark
and Sweden. But shockingly, at the other end

00:16:52.330 --> 00:17:01.400
of the spectrum was America, for quality and
health issues the USA ranked 120th out of

00:17:01.400 --> 00:17:09.830
125 countries, putting it in the same league
as Saudi Arabia, Jordan, Ethiopia and Chad.

00:17:09.830 --> 00:17:15.069
It’s one of life’s great ironies that
the world’s wealthiest superpower has some

00:17:15.069 --> 00:17:21.339
of the lowest quality food in the world. But
it’s not the fault of the American peoples,

00:17:21.339 --> 00:17:26.530
large American food companies that have monopolised
the market use every trick in the book and

00:17:26.530 --> 00:17:33.290
some horrifying techniques and chemicals to
make terribly poor quality food seem more

00:17:33.290 --> 00:17:39.300
appealing to shoppers. And in America and
some other countries, the regulations just

00:17:39.300 --> 00:17:44.280
aren’t in place to properly regulate what
goes into people’s food, at least they’re

00:17:44.280 --> 00:17:52.740
nowhere near stringent enough. But just remember,
every time you shop, you are voting. Avoiding

00:17:52.740 --> 00:18:00.290
cheap, processed and general dodgy-looking
produce will reduce the demand for it. Choosing

00:18:00.290 --> 00:18:06.590
to instead shop at local stores with real,
high quality food will make a difference,

00:18:06.590 --> 00:18:13.610
and you’ll live a longer, happier life as
well, for the sake of a bit less convenience.

00:18:13.610 --> 00:18:23.190
You wouldn’t eat garbage out the bin so
don’t settle for buying it off the shelves.

00:18:23.190 --> 00:18:36.430
Thanks for watching.

